WEBVTT

00:00.600 --> 00:02.567
(upbeat music)

00:12.333 --> 00:14.433
- Bruce Lee, super focus.

00:14.433 --> 00:15.667
Getting ready for combat.

00:17.467 --> 00:20.167
And then the camera will zoom
in 'cause it was the 70s.

00:20.167 --> 00:23.933
As a kid growing up in
Hawaii, Bruce Lee to me

00:25.133 --> 00:29.200
was the only Asian
person I ever saw

00:29.200 --> 00:33.000
in movies and TV who kicked ass.

00:33.000 --> 00:38.000
Bruce Lee was a martial artist,
movie star, philosopher,

00:39.967 --> 00:44.933
poet, man of the people, and
just another Seattle dude.

00:46.333 --> 00:49.400
He went to Garfield High School,
University of Washington,

00:49.400 --> 00:51.700
met the love of his life here.

00:51.700 --> 00:54.433
Bruce Lee started his
freshman year at U-Dub

00:54.433 --> 00:57.200
the same year that the
space needle was built.

00:57.200 --> 01:01.067
I5 construction had just
begun that very same year.

01:01.067 --> 01:05.300
The Seattle we know now,
the embryo of it started

01:05.300 --> 01:07.200
when Bruce Lee was around.

01:07.200 --> 01:09.867
It was the hip-hop
generation that created

01:09.867 --> 01:12.000
what we know now is Bruce Lee.

01:12.000 --> 01:15.233
I mean, you can see the
photoshopped Bruce Lee t-shirts,

01:15.233 --> 01:18.867
where he's like a Bruce Lee
with headphones and turntables.

01:18.867 --> 01:21.467
Every hip-hop artist who
comes to town on tour,

01:21.467 --> 01:23.800
they're not out here
catching fish at Pike Place

01:23.800 --> 01:25.367
or going on the Space Needle,

01:25.367 --> 01:27.100
they're going to
visit Bruce Lee.

01:27.100 --> 01:28.833
Seattle in the
60s, you're looking

01:28.833 --> 01:33.833
at the Civil Rights Movement
unravel all over the country,

01:35.267 --> 01:36.233
and then you're realizing
you're living in a city

01:36.233 --> 01:38.000
that itself is segregated.

01:38.000 --> 01:41.200
The carts and the stereotype
of the Asian male,

01:41.200 --> 01:45.133
which sadly still
exists to this day.

01:45.133 --> 01:48.700
The meek Asian male,
very familiar with that.

01:48.700 --> 01:50.000
I've been teased with it,

01:51.400 --> 01:54.667
but I also have thought
constantly Long Duk Dong.

01:54.667 --> 01:56.867
- What's happening, hot stuff?

01:56.867 --> 02:01.333
- You know, the kid
from Goonies, who I
wanted to root for.

02:01.333 --> 02:03.333
He was cool to me,

02:03.333 --> 02:06.367
come to find out he's the
nerd to everybody else.

02:06.367 --> 02:10.800
All those stereotypes,
I think, Bruce Lee,

02:10.800 --> 02:12.367
he was very aware of them.

02:12.367 --> 02:14.933
- That in the United
States, I think something

02:14.933 --> 02:17.933
about the Oriental,
I mean the true

02:18.933 --> 02:21.200
Oriental should be shown.

02:21.200 --> 02:23.067
- Hollywood sure as heck hasn't.

02:23.067 --> 02:24.333
- You better believe it, man.

02:24.333 --> 02:25.833
I mean, it's always the pigtail

02:25.833 --> 02:27.700
and bouncing around chop-chop

02:27.700 --> 02:29.567
with the eyes
framed and all that.

02:29.567 --> 02:32.500
- Instead of looking at the
stereotype and being like,

02:32.500 --> 02:36.400
these Asian dudes on our
screen are like sidekicks

02:36.400 --> 02:41.133
and meek people, I'm just gonna
be a bad ass all the time.

02:41.133 --> 02:43.000
Well, guess what?

02:43.000 --> 02:46.933
Now, you end up with a
whole 'nother caricature.

02:46.933 --> 02:51.933
He wrote poetry, and he
trained hard and kicked ass.

02:53.200 --> 02:56.467
He knew that the
best way to fight

02:56.467 --> 02:58.367
a one-dimensional
portrayal is to be

02:58.367 --> 03:00.567
as multidimensional as possible.

03:00.567 --> 03:03.900
I watched my
six-year-old son watch

03:03.900 --> 03:06.400
Enter the Dragon for
the very first time.

03:06.400 --> 03:10.500
He had the same exact face,
pretty sure that I had.

03:10.500 --> 03:13.500
Whenever Bruce Lee triumphed,
he was like, "Yeah, me too."

03:13.500 --> 03:14.867
To see someone

03:17.233 --> 03:20.500
for that community,
for that identity,

03:20.500 --> 03:22.933
for that racialized
identity was important.

03:22.933 --> 03:25.767
So, long story short,
Bruce Lee made it

03:25.767 --> 03:29.500
a little more cooler
to be an Asian dude.

03:29.500 --> 03:32.500
There's a mythology
that surrounds him

03:32.500 --> 03:34.900
and his legacy and
what he represented.

03:34.900 --> 03:38.433
He symbolized what can be done

03:38.433 --> 03:42.867
as an Asian male
growing up in America.

03:42.867 --> 03:45.467
(upbeat music)
